    "text": "<p>For a concentrated solution of a weak electrolyte&nbsp;(<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi>eq</mi></msub><mo>=</mo></math>equilibrium constant) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;of concentration&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8216;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>&#8217;</mo><mo>,</mo></math> the degree of dissociation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8216;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi><mo>&#8217;</mo></math>&nbsp;is</p>"
